* Partial\nnotes
** The constraint
*** Private functions cannot\nread current public state
*** A swap price exists only\nat execution time
*** A note needs its value\nat creation
*** Private then public,\nnever back
** Two-phase\ncommitment
*** partial = H(owner,\nrandomness)
*** note_hash = H(slot,\npartial, value)
*** Private half fixes\nwho gets paid
*** Public half fixes\nhow much
*** Every Aztec note uses\nthis format internally
** The completer
*** Commitment alone is\njust a Field, copyable
*** Validity commitment\nH(partial, completer)
*** Written to the\nnullifier tree
*** Own domain separator,\nconsumes nothing
*** Creator fixes payee\nand finaliser
** Single use
*** Protocol does not\nenforce it
*** Reuse links completions\nvia the shared tag
*** PXE drops the pending\nentry after the first
*** A second payment is\nmost likely lost
** Completion\ncontext
*** complete\npublic, amount visible
*** complete_from_private\ntag-gated private log
*** Amount is hidden only\nif the commitment is
*** Private completion needs\na prior settled tx
** DeFi use
*** AMM swap at an\nonchain exchange rate
*** Interest accrual,\ngas-dependent values
*** AIP-20 commitment\ntransfers
*** AIP-4626 vault shares
** Payment\nendpoints
*** Name maps to commitments,\nnot to an address
*** Relayer contract as\nuniversal completer
*** Authwit lets the relayer\ndebit the sender
*** Offchain or onchain\nlookup channel
*** Not a stealth\naddress scheme
** What leaks
*** The relayer was called
*** One completion tag\nper payment
*** Refill cadence, if\ncreation is visible
*** Public completion\nreveals the amount
@endmindmap
